{"id":2540187,"name":"Breast Size Slider  - (Krea-2 + ZIT)","description":"<h1 id=\"krea-2-v2:\"><span style=\"color:rgb(64, 192, 87)\">Krea-2 </span>V2:</h1><p><span style=\"color:rgb(21, 170, 191)\"><strong>V2 is focused on stability, and on keeping the womans body unaffected in size. Most, if not all other Breast size slider will make every woman chubby when you increase breast size, but this LoRA will keep the rest of her body lean and almost unaffected, in both directions.</strong></span><br />It behaves different with and without clothes. And with different LoRA combinations etc. But in general i would stay within these values:</p><h2 id=\"range-naked:-5-to-5range-with-clothes:-5-to-8\">Range <span style=\"color:rgb(250, 176, 5)\"><em>naked</em></span>: <span style=\"color:rgb(250, 82, 82)\">-5</span> to <span style=\"color:rgb(64, 192, 87)\">5</span><br />Range <span style=\"color:rgb(190, 75, 219)\"><em>with clothes</em></span>: <span style=\"color:rgb(250, 82, 82)\">-5</span> to <span style=\"color:rgb(64, 192, 87)\">8</span></h2><p><strong>If you want </strong><span style=\"color:rgb(250, 82, 82)\"><strong>hyper</strong></span><strong>, or have problems with</strong><span style=\"color:rgb(250, 82, 82)\"><strong> large breasts getting a forced bra,</strong></span><strong> use</strong><span style=\"color:rgb(64, 192, 87)\"><strong> <u>V1</u> and <u>V2</u> combined</strong></span><strong> at half strength.</strong></p><hr /><h3 id=\"krea-2-v1:\"><span style=\"color:rgb(134, 142, 150)\">Krea-2 V1:</span></h3><h3 id=\"recommended-range:-4-to-5\"><span style=\"color:rgb(134, 142, 150)\">Recommended range: -4 to 5</span></h3><hr /><p></p><h1 id=\"zit\"><span style=\"color:rgb(250, 82, 82)\"><strong>ZIT</strong></span></h1><p><span style=\"color:rgb(253, 126, 20)\">v1.1</span> is <span style=\"color:rgb(250, 176, 5)\">v1.0</span> merged 50/50 with a <span style=\"color:rgb(250, 82, 82)\">v2.0</span> candidate that i didnt think would live up to a <span style=\"color:rgb(250, 82, 82)\">v2.0</span> quality.<br /><span style=\"color:rgb(64, 192, 87)\">Pros </span>of <span style=\"color:rgb(253, 126, 20)\">v1.1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(64, 192, 87)\"> </span>is that is retains the <span style=\"color:rgb(64, 192, 87)\">original face, light and pose better</span>. And therefor it can also be pushed to higher values. <br />I also changed the name of the LoRA to \"Breast\" instead of \"Breast<span style=\"color:rgb(250, 82, 82)\">s</span>\", both here in civ and the filename.</p><h2 id=\"recommended-range:-3.0-to-10.0\"><br />Recommended range: <span style=\"color:rgb(250, 82, 82)\">-3.0</span> to <span style=\"color:rgb(64, 192, 87)\">10.0</span></h2><p></p><hr /><p>All my work is 100% free. <span style=\"color:rgb(21, 170, 191)\">The only thing that really matters to me is people leaving a review</span>, <span style=\"color:rgb(64, 192, 87)\">good </span>or <span style=\"color:rgb(250, 82, 82)\">bad</span>. I will NEVER remove or block anyone for leaving a bad review, so don't be afraid to give me criticism.</p><p>I'm stating this because when a creator blocks someone for leaving a bad review, that person can no longer see any of the creator's models, essentially muting their critics. This is something I'm highly critical of, and I believe it's a fundamental quality problem on this site.</p>","allowNoCredit":false,"allowCommercialUse":["Image","RentCivit"],"allowDerivatives":false,"allowDifferentLicense":false,"type":"LORA","minor":false,"sfwOnly":false,"poi":false,"nsfw":true,"nsfwLevel":60,"availability":"Public","userId":8269905,"hasActivePaidAccess":false,"baseModels":["Krea 2","ZImageTurbo"],"cosmetic":null,"supportsGeneration":true,"stats":{"downloadCount":37506,"thumbsUpCount":1580,"thumbsDownCount":0,"commentCount":25,"tippedAmountCount":125},"creator":{"username":"Loraholic","image":"https://image.civitai.com/xG1nkqKTMzGDvpLrqFT7WA/602dc520-64d0-463f-899e-fc4db661834e/width=96/Loraholic.jpeg"},"tags":["bustaholic",